# Documentation

- **Single canonical tree:** All SilverKey long-form prose lives under **`documentation/`** at the repo root. See `documentation/README.md` and `documentation/how-we-document.md`.
- **Repo-root `docs/` must not exist.** Do not create it. If you see broken links to `docs/`, retarget to `documentation/runbooks/` for Postgres/Redis/Celery ops. **Creating `docs/` at repo root fails CI** (`scripts/ci/check-doc-placement.sh`).
- **Hubs (Diataxis):** `getting-started/`, `architecture/`, `features/`, `guides/`, `reference/`, `runbooks/`, `policies/`, `internal/`.
- **As-built only:** No roadmap or Planned design trees in-repo. Track planned work in Linear.
- **Colocated exception only:** `*/docs/` inside vendor-owned subtrees (e.g. `Server/app/services/docusign/docs/`).
- **FORBIDDEN paths for new long-form guides:** repo-root `docs/`, `Client/documentation/`, ad-hoc long `.md` in feature folders (use `documentation/features/` instead).
- **Lightweight READMEs:** Major folders keep short READMEs that link into `documentation/`.
- **Adding docs:** Place under the correct hub; add a row to that hub’s README. Run `scripts/ci/check-doc-placement.sh` and `scripts/ci/check-doc-links.sh` (`make check-docs`). Skill: `.cursor/skills/documentation-placement/SKILL.md`.
- **Major feature or architecture change:** [documentation/internal/post-major-change-checklist.md](../../../documentation/internal/post-major-change-checklist.md) and skill **post-major-change-sync**.
- **Team-maintained exceptions (no surprise markdown):** `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `setup.md`, `.cursor/README.md`, `documentation/internal/**`, `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
